@vsm 1.0
// system_assessment_2026-06-02.vsm — what the ℝ¹²⁸ vectors mean, parameter calibration
// status, component maturity scorecard, and the detailed remaining-task ledger.
// domain_context: {target=vsf-nucleus, env=assessment, layer=S3}
// markers: ✓ confirmed/done | ◐ partial | ◯ not done | ? unknown   (rigor protocol)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// 1. WHAT THE ℝ¹²⁸ VECTORS ARE  (and 282 vs 3043)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

state_vector_meaning:
  "Each vector x(t) ∈ ℝ¹²⁸ is ONE full snapshot of the kernel's state at tick t.
   The 128 coordinates are NOT free — they are 8 named blocks (state_vector.rs):
     A 0..15   health     — trust_history[0..9], dtrust, error_rate, absorption, governed, depth, lifecycle
     B 16..23  resources  — cpu/mem/io pressure, budget, cgroup_headroom, child_count, queue φ↑/φ↓
     C 24..31  entropy    — H_t, H_rest, dH, entropy_phase, stasis_cos, soplo_active, n_cycles, ticks_growth
     D 32..47  organelles — mem_mgr, io_router, sig_relay, scheduler activations (+ reserved)
     E 48..63  VSL        — φ↑/φ↓ rate, algedonic, psi_active, escalation
     F 64..95  attractor  — stasis_vec_prev[64..79] + stasis_vec_curr[80..95]
     G 96..127 learning   — V_ref compressed, Δ|pattern|, λ, RAP
   So a 'trajectory' = the kernel's path through this 128-D state space over time."

effective_dimensionality:
  "D_KY ≈ 3.00 (confirmed, multiple runs). Although the space is 128-D, the dynamics live on a
   ~3-D submanifold — only ~3 directions are 'active'. THIS is why PCA→3D works and why raw-cosine
   does not suffer curse-of-dimensionality (EXP-TDA-01 H_TDA2). Most of the 128 coords are near-constant
   or sparsely populated in spec_boot (D/E/F/G barely move without real load)."

n282_vs_n3043:
  "Same kernel, two SAMPLING regimes of the SAME trajectory:
     282  = status=stasis_vector — emitted ONLY when entropy_phase=='stasis' (the converged fixed
            point). Tight cluster (mean dist to centroid 0.258). They are repeated near-samples of the
            ONE attractor point ⇒ trivially β₀=1, β₁=0.
     3043 = status=traj_vector (VSF_DUMP_EVERY_TICK) — EVERY tick, ALL phases (stasis/inhale/degen/
            exhale + the initial transient). Spread 0.786, stasis_cos 0.61–1.00. The 282 stasis points
            are ⊂ the stasis-phase portion of the 3043; the extra ~2761 are the breathing excursions +
            transient. THIS is the geometry the TDA calibration actually needed."

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// 2. WHICH VECTORS ARE STILL MISSING  (regimes not yet sampled)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

missing_vectors:
  perturbation:   "◯ thermal/activation KICK episodes — for H_TDA3 (β₁ spike + recovery). spec_boot's
                   gentle entropy cycle never leaves the basin. Need thermal_ceiling_v4_bis or a delta-kick
                   run with VSF_DUMP_EVERY_TICK."
  real_S1_load:   "◯ real workload variety. The live daemon's VAR-1/TRUST-1 are STILL synthetic constants
                   (record_variety(0.05)/record_trust(0.95)); Blocks D/E/G barely move. Need real BBH/S1
                   variety → populates the dormant dimensions (gated by R6: internal-first)."
  coupled_joint:  "◯ ℝ²⁵⁶ joint trajectories from ψ-coupling (F5.x.6) — no multi-kernel run yet."
  live_dynamics:  "◯ the LIVE daemon does NOT step the operator/stasis — kernel_tick only fills Block B
                   (ingest) + checks Ω. So no live L-trajectory exists for lyapunov/vr_complex to consume."
  adversarial:    "◐ NC controls exist (EXP-NC-*) but not re-run against the current kernel."
  senescence:     "◐ EXP-TSM 240min done; adaptive H_rest senescence (EXP-SEN-01) is a seed."

